    "Iteration-2: with-skill now 100% (33/33), up from 97%. The iteration-1 fixes all held: every run made links bidirectional (closing the eval-1 one-way miss), dropped openings whose target room had no panorama instead of dangling, and used the wider floor band. The Vatika agent again caught the scrambled filenames (4/6 wrong) and classified from pixels.",
    "Baseline carried over from iteration-1 unchanged (no-skill baseline is stable for a new skill): 75.8% with high variance, two runs producing non-portable custom schemas.",
    "Remaining minor friction (polish, not blocking): (a) floor-band boundary - prose allows far open-plan pucks at -15..-22 but the verifier warns shallower than -12, and one far great-room opening wanted ~-11; consider allowing shallower for open_archway types. (b) overlays are named by scene id not image filename - one agent hit a failed Read. (c) 'two panoramas of one open volume' / which hub owns a shared opening is still judgment-heavy. (d) a one-line note that panoramas may not be exactly 2:1 (overlay uses real dims)."
